{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794322855,"nonce":"egzJWITPgc2nrMcba071PtabxQk=","title":"Fiber transform: an if with a computed condition around a resume point stops the rewrite","message":"add_rewind_dispatch plans, per function, how many spill locals of each type it needs, and the rewrite then asks for them (spill_stack). Entering an if whose condition is not a plain local.get or constant needs that condition spilled, and the plan recorded the spill count for the frame entry but never added its operand types to the reserved pool; only call sites contributed. Such a function stopped the whole link with 'the plan reserved 0 locals of I32 and the rewrite wants 1', with no function named. Found with a function emitted by the direct wasm backend (a1e1488): a poll written as 'load epoch; local.tee; local.get; i64.ne; if { call hlp_fiber_poll }'. LLVM's code rarely has the shape, since its conditions are usually branches.\n\nFix: Enclosing carries the types its entry spills (entry_need) and the pool takes them when a resume point inside makes that entry a boundary. The error now names the function (module index) and operator offset. Test: an_if_whose_condition_is_computed_is_planned_and_runs. That test's driver jumps without saving or restoring, so rewinding through the spilled condition is exercised by the end-to-end fiber tests (wasm_direct_mixed with ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1).","files":null}]}